The Architectural Review is a monthly international <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architecture">architectural</a> magazine published in <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London">London</a> since 1896. Articles cover the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Built_environment">built environment</a> which includes <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landscape">landscape</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Building_design">building design</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interior_design">interior design</a> and <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urbanism">urbanism</a> as well as theory of these subjects.

&nbsp;

The publishers, Emap Construct, also produce a sister publication called <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architects_Journal">Architects' Journal</a>.
